<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39521" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmōnĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the lungs</i>, <i>pulmonic</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulmoneum vomitum vomere,</span>”
				<i>to vomit up the lungs</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Rud. 2, 6, 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>soft</i> or <i>swelling like the lungs</i>, <i>spongy</i>: pedes, v. l. ap. <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ep.
				5, 1, 21</span></i> (al. pulmon'es): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 14, 15, § 52</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
